rt text Plain Text\nexport endnote Endnote (file)\nexport refworks Refworks\n\nRequest / recall this title\n(2-3 business days)\n[Cover--Click to expand.]\n[Add this title to your marked items list]\nAdd\nA humument : a treated Victorian novel\nTom Phillips.\nAuthor: \tPhillips, Tom, 1937- author.\nPublished: \tLondon : Thames & Hudson Ltd, 2016.\nCopyright: \t©2016\nEdition: \tFinal edition.\nDescription: \t367 pages : color illustrations ; 18 cm\nFormat: \tBook\nSummary:\nIn 1966, Tom Phillips took a forgotten nineteenth-century novel, W. H. Mallock's A Human Document, and began working over the extant text to create something new.The artist writes, \"I plundered, mined , and undermined its text to make it yield the ghosts of other possible stories, scenes, poems, erotic incidents, and surrealist catastrophes which seemed to lurk within its wall of words. As I worked on it, I replaced the text I'd stripped away with visual images of all kinds. It began to tell and depict, among other memories, dreams, and reflections, the sad story of Bill Toge, one of love's casualties.\"After its first publication in book form in 1980, A Humument rapidly became a cult classic. This sixth and final edition, published to celebrate the fiftieth anniversary of Tom Phillips' first experiments with A Human Document, presents for the first time an entirely revised and complete version of A Humument , and will bring to a close half a century's artistic endeavor.\nContent provided by Syndetic Solutions, Inc. Terms of Use\n... ( see more )\n\n    Subjects\n    Location\n    MARC\n    Full Record\n\nSubjects\nPhillips, Tom, 1937-\nMallock, W. H. (William Hurrell), 1849-1923 -- Adaptations.\nLiterature, Experimental.\nCHR 2016.\nPRO Phillips, Tom, 1937- (autograph) (RBC copy)\n\nOther Title: \tHuman document.\nRelated Works: \tMallock, W. H. (William Hurrell), 1849-1923. Human document.\nOther Author: \tMallock, W. H. (William Hurrell), 1849-1923.\nLocation\nOnline\nLocation \tCall # \tStat